# canary: the only wrong TRUE the corpus ever produced (#51). BMC explored an
# impossible branch after an undecided feasibility check, found every path
# below it contradictory, explored nothing, and still discharged 62 obligations
# -- including an unconditional out-of-bounds read -- as exhaustively proven.
# Expected FALSE; UNKNOWN is honest and scores as unproven, TRUE means the
# completeness claim has come back.
sv-comp/argv-tasks/Pan_exceptionprone.yml no-runtime-exception

# canaries: the seeded-precondition guard let the BMC treat a call as
# non-throwing because its preconditions were emitted as obligations -- while
# under valid-assert those obligations are not consumed at all, so nothing
# carried the burden. Eight wrong TRUEs. The flag that says whether they are
# seeded was computed for a decision record and never stored, so it sat at its
# default for every property.
sv-comp/securibench/Basic29.yml valid-assert
sv-comp/securibench/Basic30.yml valid-assert
sv-comp/securibench/Datastructures5.yml valid-assert
sv-comp/securibench/Factories3.yml valid-assert
sv-comp/securibench/Inter4.yml valid-assert
